.Dd July 18, 2026
.Dt ICE 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ice
.Nd Intel E810 Ethernet Device Driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/net/ice*
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver is a GLDv3, multi-threaded, clonable, loadable device driver that
supports the Data Link Provider Interface,
.Xr dlpi 4P ,
on the Intel E810 family of Ethernet controllers.
.Pp
The controller negotiates its rate with the attached media and supported
speeds range from 1 GbE through 100 GbE depending on the installed
transceiver or cable.
.Pp
In addition to basic device initialization and the sending and receiving of
frames, the driver supports the following features:
.Bl -dash -offset indent
.It
Jumbo frames up to 9706 bytes.
.It
Promiscuous access via
.Xr snoop 8
and
.Xr dlpi 4P .
.It
IPv4 header checksum offload.
.It
IPv4 and IPv6 TCP, UDP checksum offload.
.It
Receive Side Scaling
.Pq RSS
across multiple hardware queues.
.It
TCP Segmentation Offload
.Pq LSO ,
disabled by default; see
.Sx PROPERTIES .
.It
Transceiver information through
.Xr dladm 8 .
.El
.Pp
The
.Nm
driver does not currently support hardware VLAN filtering offload, energy
efficient Ethernet
.Pq EEE ,
SR-IOV, or hardware flow control through pause frames.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The
.Nm
driver is configured by defining properties in its
.Xr driver.conf 5
file
.Pa /kernel/drv/ice.conf .
Values there apply to all
.Nm
instances; the properties are described in
.Sx PROPERTIES .
The maximum transmission unit and other data-link properties may also be set
at runtime with
.Xr dladm 8 .
.Pp
The driver requires the Dynamic Device Personalization
.Pq DDP
package installed at
.Pa /kernel/firmware/ice/ice.pkg .
If the package cannot be loaded the device enters a reduced-function safe mode
with a single queue.
.Sh PROPERTIES
The following properties may be set in the
.Nm
.Xr driver.conf 5
file.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy num_queues
The number of receive and transmit data queues to allocate.
The value is clamped to the number of online CPUs and the number of MSI-X
interrupt vectors the platform grants, and is rounded down to a power of two.
The default is the driver maximum.
.It Sy tx_lso_enable
When set to a non-zero value, the driver advertises TCP large-send (LSO/TSO)
segmentation offload.
The default is
.Sy 0
.Pq disabled .
.It Sy default_mtu
The initial maximum transmission unit, in bytes.
The MTU may also be changed at runtime with
.Xr dladm 8 .
The default is
.Sy 1500 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /dev/net/ice*
Per-instance character-special device.
.It Pa /kernel/drv/amd64/ice
Device driver
.Pq 64-bit .
.It Pa /kernel/drv/ice.conf
Driver configuration file.
.It Pa /kernel/firmware/ice/ice.pkg
Dynamic Device Personalization package.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dlpi 4P ,
.Xr driver.conf 5 ,
.Xr dladm 8 ,
.Xr snoop 8
